From: TuxRGB
Subject: [PATCH] Build with MinGW-w64 (Windows)

TuxRGB builds OpenRGB for Windows with MinGW-w64, from Linux
(scripts/windows/build-openrgb-windows.sh), so that the Windows installer
carries the same engine as the AppImage, with patch 0001. One source change
is needed: hueplusplus converts UTC timestamps with _mkgmtime() under MSVC
and with setenv("TZ")/mktime() elsewhere; MinGW-w64 has _mkgmtime() but no
setenv(). The other MSVC differences (compiler flag, prebuilt MSVC
libraries, comsupp.lib, header names written with capitals) are handled by
the build script, without touching the sources. Nothing changes on Linux.

--- a/dependencies/hueplusplus-1.2.0/src/TimePattern.cpp
+++ b/dependencies/hueplusplus-1.2.0/src/TimePattern.cpp
@@ -90,7 +90,8 @@
 std::chrono::system_clock::time_point parseUTCTimestamp(const std::string& timestamp)
 {
     std::tm tm = timestampToTm(timestamp);
-#ifdef _MSC_VER
+    // Modified by TuxRGB (2026-11-01): MinGW-w64 has _mkgmtime too, not setenv.
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) || defined(__MINGW32__)
     std::time_t ctime = _mkgmtime(&tm);
 #else
     // Non-standard, but POSIX compliant
